  "build_notes": "`build.pad_to_bytes`: the 8x8 PNG of the first case followed by zero bytes up to that many decoded bytes (trailing bytes after the last PNG chunk, which a decoder ignores). `build.png_dims`: a PNG signature and IHDR claiming [width, height] with no pixel data, which is refused on the header alone, before any decode. `build.png_text_chunk`: the 8x8 PNG with a `zTXt`, `iTXt` (compression flag 1) or `iCCP` chunk, before IDAT, that is valid zlib and inflates to that many zero bytes (a few KB on the wire). Always refused as `unreadable_image` when it inflates to more than `max_metadata_inflated_bytes`, even if the decoder would skip the chunk; the check is an inflate that stops at max + 1 bytes. `exif_gps`: the JPEG has an EXIF APP1 whose IFD0 points (tag 0x8825) to a GPS IFD with a latitude and longitude; after the server re-encodes, the output must hold no APP1/Exif segment and no 0x8825 tag. `jpeg_dims`: the JPEG's SOF0 claims [width, height] and is refused on the header. Orientation: only a JPEG's EXIF orientation is applied; a PNG `eXIf` chunk is ignored (the app sends JPEG, #989), so no case turns a PNG.",
  "max_metadata_inflated_bytes": 65536
}
